# Environment-dependent example: reports selected service processes visible in
# this Linux host. The process sets are typed values, not parsed stdout from
# ps, pgrep, or awk; show and summarize read the same bounded snapshot.
#
# Bash would need separate commands, quoting, and text parsing to produce a
# similar report. yesh keeps process identity, fields, and RSS arithmetic
# explicit. The example is read-only: it does not signal or modify processes.

# Role of yesh: select and report a bounded process view; the kernel and procfs remain the sources of state.
sshd = processes where name is "sshd"
show $sshd fields pid ppid uid state rss start_time cgroup
summarize $sshd memory rss

nginx = processes where name is "nginx"
show $nginx fields pid ppid uid state rss start_time cgroup
summarize $nginx memory rss
